        "en" to GemDetails(
            "Topaz is a fluorinated aluminium silicate that crystallises in pegmatites and greisens, granitic rocks transformed by fluorine-rich fluids, and in rhyolites. Naturally blue topaz exists, pale, coloured by defects due to weak natural radioactivity. But almost all vivid blue topaz on the market is colourless topaz that has been irradiated and then heated: irradiation creates brown and blue colour centres, and heating removes the brown and stabilises the blue. The tints carry trade names: “Sky Blue”, “Swiss Blue”, “London Blue”.",
